# --- s032 Book I d.7 q.1 = Ord. I d.7 q.1 (Vat. IV)
n("n554","s032-01","Circa septimam distinctionem","la","source","= Scotus, *Ord.* I d. 7 q. 1 (ed. Vat. IV), *utrum potentia generandi in Patre sit aliquid absolutum vel relatio*. Cf. Lombard, *Sent.* I d. 7.","certain")
n("n555","s032-01","eo enim est pater quo est filius","la","source","Augustine, *De Trin.*: the dictum that the Father is Father by that by which he has a Son (cf. *De Trin.* VII 1.2 and V 6.7). A and B (*xv.*) agree on book XV; the locus is to be checked.","to-verify")
n("n556","s032-01","ergo eo","la","textual","A reads *ergo eo* at the line-end and then *est pater quo generat* at the top of p. 53. B has *ergo eo pater quo generat* (B checked).","certain")
n("n557","s032-01","li. 1. c. 8.","la","source","John Damascene, *De fide orthodoxa* I c. 8 (B *li. i. c. viij.*).","certain")
n("n558","s032-02","pedis","la","textual","So A and B (*pedis qstionis*, B checked). Apparently ‘at the foot’ (start) of the question, i.e. at the head of the body of the question after the arguments. No correction is suggested.","uncertain")
n("n559","s032-02","q. 40. articulo. 5.","la","source","The view that the *potentia generandi* signifies the essence directly is Aquinas, *ST* I q. 41 a. 5 (*utrum potentia generandi significet relationem vel essentiam*). A has *q. 40*, B *q. iiij.*; both are wrong.","to-verify")
n("n560","s032-02","quodlibeto. 3°. q. 5.","la","textual","B: *quolib. iij. q. iij.* (B checked). Henry of Ghent, *Quodl.* III; the right question is to be checked. Both agree on *Summa* a. 57 q. 7.","to-verify")
n("n561","s032-03","5°. metha.","la","source","Aristotle, *Metaph.* V.12, 1019b21–33 (*possibile* in the logical sense, i.e. non-contradiction of terms).","certain")
n("n562","s032-03","4. metha.","la","source","The division of being by act and potency is *Metaph.* V.7, 1017a35–b9, and IX.1. *Metaph.* IV is presumably a slip.","to-verify")
n("n563","s032-03","Tunc doctor soluit questionem. et tenet duas conclusiones","la","source","Scotus's answer: the *potentia generandi*, taken for what it denominates *per se* (its proximate foundation), is something absolute, namely the divine essence as *memoria fecunda* in the Father. The relation is co-signified. Cf. *Ord.* I d. 7 q. 1.","to-verify")
n("n564","s032-05","prehabet terminum adequatum","la","source","Why the Son, who has the same fruitful memory, does not beget, and why there cannot be several Sons: the power is exhausted by its adequate term. Cf. *Ord.* I d. 7 q. 2 (*utrum in divinis possint esse plures filii*), which Gorris folds into q. 1.","to-verify")
n("n565","s032-06","generatio in diuinis est vniuoca","la","source","*Ord.* I d. 7 q. 1: divine generation as univocal production, in which the offspring is like the begetter in nature.","to-verify")
n("n566","s032-06","vt querit questio","la","textual","So A (abbreviated *ꝙrit. q.*) and B (*vt querit questio*, B checked).","certain")
n("n567","s032-02","at the foot of the question","en","translation","Lat. *pedis questionis*; see the Latin note.")
n("n568","s032-03","logical power","en","translation","*potentia logica*: possibility as mere non-repugnance of the terms, as opposed to real (active or passive) power.")
n("n569","s032-04","repugnance of terms","en","translation","*repugnantia terminorum*: a ‘Son begetting’ would require a term (a second Son) whose existence is impossible.")

